<p>From <a href="https://x.com/MerriamWebster">Merriam-Webster&#8217;s Twitter feed</a>:</p>
<p>Vitamin C is also called ascorbic acid.</p>
<p>The Greek-derived prefix <em>a-</em> means &#8220;not, without.&#8221;</p>
<p><em>Scorbutus</em> in New Latin means &#8220;scurvy.&#8221;</p>
<p>So ascorbic acid is &#8220;no-scurvy acid.&#8221;</p>
